AB  - Troubleshooting and fault detection by identifying root causes of issues is a key activity in IT Operations when maintaining large, complex systems. During the past few years, AI for IT Operations (AIOps), and specifically AI agents that leverage large language models (LLMs) for IT Operations (LLMOps) have been gathering steam. In this article, we present the cornerstone for our pedagogy-based approach to gain a deeper understanding of the current state of LLMOps capabilities. We highlight that while LLMs have made significant advances, they are still not a silver bullet in solving operational challenges. Furthermore, we draw attention to the shortcomings of metrics such as pass@k and pass ${ }^{\wedge} k$, and motivate the need for better metrics.
