AB  - AI-driven remediation agents that autonomously diagnose and repair faults in cloud microservice systems are becoming integral to modern IT operations. However, the telemetry these agents rely on—metrics, logs, and traces—can be corrupted by adversarial manipulation or environmental noise, leading to harmful recovery actions. We propose SafeRemed, a safety-aware remediation framework that inserts a Safety Policy Layer between diagnosis and action execution. SafeRemed comprises a Telemetry Authenticity Estimator (TAE) that quantifies telemetry trustworthiness through structural, cross-modal, and temporal verification, and an Action Risk Gate (ARG) that enforces tiered authorization so that only low-risk actions proceed autonomously under uncertain conditions. We evaluate SafeRemed on the AIOpsLab benchmark with the DeathStarBench SocialNetwork application under benign, noisy, and adversarial conditions. SafeRemed reduces the unsafe action rate by up to 79.4% while maintaining acceptable remediation success, and achieves a defense success rate of 0.72–0.88 across diverse attack types. Our results demonstrate that explicit safety gating is a practical and important component for LLM-based AIOps agents, though it introduces moderate latency overhead in benign scenarios.
ER  - 

