AB  - This study examines how Artificial Intelligence (AI) transforms the cloud infrastructure provisioning process, a fundamental element of contemporary IT management. Organizations can move from reactive cloud operations to predictive self-optimizing environments through a combination of machine learning (ML) models with observability tools, AWS CloudWatch, and the Terraform declarative infrastructure-ascode (IaC) framework. This study provides a detailed analysis of the technologies and architectural principles involved, along with operational advantages, strategic insights, and real-world implementation examples. This study identifies three main obstacles: data quality issues, model interpretability problems, and vendor lock-in challenges, and provides solutions to address them. The combination of MLOps and AIOps enables organizations to achieve substantial benefits in terms of cost optimization, performance improvement, system reliability, and deployment agility.
