AB  - For urban airside inspection and emergency distribution, this is continuous operation, and this research proposes an end-to-end low-altitude intelligent operation and maintenance system architecture, connecting perception, network, platform and application four layers in series. System adopts MAVLink, OPC UA and Remote ID for unified telemetry, while relying on 5G RedCap and TSN/PTP to ensure millisecond-level jitter, with edge-region fusion and AIOps orchestration supporting state monitoring, predictive maintenance, path planning and collaborative scheduling. In Suzhou Industrial Park SMT chip production line, empirical verification shows that unplanned downtime reduced by 30%, and daily production capacity increased by 25%, while operation and maintenance cost reduced by 30%, with delay from alarm to scheduling being reduced by 62.5%, thereby shortening work order closed-loop time by 33.3%. At same time, technical innovation index increased by 40%, and labor productivity increased by 28%, while energy consumption per unit output reduced by 20%. System verified adaptability under complex meteorological and electromagnetic environments in State Grid transmission corridor scenario, thereby proposing optimization paths such as RAIM and VIO fusion positioning, drift detection and incremental update. System provides reusable methodology and engineering framework for organized increment of new quality productivity.
