AB  - Telecom networks generate overwhelming alarm volumes that exceed rule-based management. We present Alarm Pattern Recognition (APR), an end-to-end AIOps framework that converts high-volume alarm streams into prioritized, interpretable patterns. APR mines temporally consistent closed co-occurrences, generalizes recurring sequences across equipment classes, and ranks them with a Noise Reduction Ratio (R2) emphasizing non-random signal. On two CSP datasets (7.4M and 9.4M events), APR consolidates 39,011 sequences into 21,205 actionable patterns and shows that the top 20% account for 33% of total signal strength. The system operates across vendors and domains and provides compact artifacts for triage, labeling, and automation—forming a scalable basis for autonomous operations
