AB  - Cloud computing is a significant revolution and an inevitable trend in the development of information technology and its core is the dynamic and rapid supply of computing, storage, and network resources on demand. This paper reports an innovative Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps) strategy, integrating an efficient storage resource capacity prediction method with a virtual machine (VM) disk scheduling method so as to improve the utilization efficiency of storage resources and promote their sustainable development. Here, a storage resource pool contains many VM disks. Specifically, a storage resource pool utilization capacity prognostic model is first proposed to predict the time when the used capacity of a storage resource pool reaches a threshold so as to give an alarm to VM disk scheduling analysis. Then, a multi-objective programming based VM disk scheduling method is established for intelligent scheduling of VM disks. Industrial cloud storage resource data have been studied to verify the proposed methodology and show that the proposed methodology can accurately predict storage resource pool utilization capacity and perform intelligent and efficient VM disk scheduling, thus ensuring efficient cloud storage resource utilization, reducing energy consumption and carbon footprints brought about by over-provisioning of resource, which provides a basis for cloud storage resource sustainable development.
ER  - 

