AB  - Modern enterprise software delivery organizations have a chronic conflict between high-velocity DevOps deployment cadences and the governance rigor prescribed within ITIL-aligned change management frameworks. Machine learning-based risk prediction models show great promise for automating change governance decisions but existing research offers little specificity on the enterprise platforms which operationalize such models at scale. Here we introduce a ServiceNow-first architecture for predictive change management where ServiceNow becomes the end-to-end orchestration layer encompassing all five functional tiers of an ML-driven risk assessment pipeline: data ingestion, feature engineering, model inference, risk scoring and decision enforcement in the pipeline. In this architecture, ServiceNow becomes the main System of Record, providing historical incident records, CMDB telemetry as well as deployment logs delivered through DataStream actions and Kafka integrations. An ensemble of Random Forest, Gradient Boosting & LSTM networks learned over 24,680 enterprise change events reaches AUC-ROC 0.947 and F1-Score 90.0% a 48% than rule-based baselines. Risk scores are generated in real-time and automatically sent into ServiceNow’s DevOps Change Velocity module using REST APIs, where Low-Risk changes (~ 60% of all pipeline events) can immediately be approved and High-Risk changes routed for prioritized human review, completely displacing traditional Change Advisory Board processes. The Model Inference Layer is hosted within ServiceNow's Predictive Intelligence and AIOps modules correlating temporal deployment observables across multi-tenant infrastructure. ServiceNow Performance Analytics Dashboards surface SHAP-based interpretability rankings for audit in regulated environments. Operational outcomes confirm 41.3% fewer changes caused incidents, and a 18.7% reduction in deployment lead time, making ServiceNow an intelligent and scalable change governance orchestrator for enterprise DevOps pipelines.
ER  - 

