AB  - Cloud Computing is the backbone of most businesses today because it provides scalable and flexible computing services at a cost-effective pric e. In addition to the traditional ways of utilizing Cloud Computing, we are starting to see the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies in existing Cloud environments. This article will discuss many aspects of Cloud Computing including service models, virtualisation, fault tolerance, business models and user experience. The article will also discuss how AI technology can enhance Cloud environments through automation, predictive analytics, improved data management, and tools such as Chatbot and AIOps. The combination of AI with Cloud Computing will increase productivity, reliability, and accuracy in decision-making and will support advanced workloads for businesses that they cannot support on their own. Nevertheless, there are still challenges associated with this combination: data privacy, algorithmic complexity, latency and vendor lock-in.
