AB  - Root Cause Analysis (RCA) remains challenging in complex and large-scale microservice architectures. The complex fault propagation among microservices and the high dimensionality of telemetry data, including metrics, logs, and traces, limit the effectiveness of existing RCA methods. In this paper, we propose an LLM-based RCA framework, termed AHF-LLM, which employs an Anchor-Guided Hierarchical Fusion (AHF) mechanism to integrate multi-source telemetry data. The contextual reasoning capability of large language models is leveraged to model temporal and cross-microservice causal dependencies. Experimental results on the CCF AIOps dataset demonstrate that AHF-LLM achieves strong performance in terms of both root cause localization accuracy and reasoning efficiency.
