AB  - World-class water transport hubs require efficient and intelligent navigation management to achieve optimal waterway transport. This study proposes an Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps) system integrating digital twin and knowledge graph technologies to address challenges such as low efficiency in traditional manual operations and prolonged fault recovery times. The system constructs a navigation scenario knowledge graph through a top-down and bottom-up hybrid approach, employing a BERTbased model to dynamically extract entity relationships from multi-source data. By incorporating digital twin technology, a 3D model is established to achieve real-time mapping of physical entities' operational status and behavioral patterns, enabling fault prediction and visual monitoring. Practical applications demonstrate that the system can rapidly localize the root causes of network resource failures, optimize operational workflows, and significantly enhance the efficiency and intelligence of navigation equipment management. The proposed framework provides a scalable technical pathway for smart operations and maintenance in large-scale hydro-junctions, offering substantial practical value for advancing intelligent transformation in waterway transportation systems.
